* MOS junction-diode structures (di_bd_area, di_bd_perim, di_bs_area, di_bs_perim).
*
* The test structure is one junction: the drain (di_bd) or the source (di_bs) diffusion
* against the bulk. The PDK subcircuit is a transistor, so D, G and S are all connected to
* the swept junction node: the stand-in channel then carries no current (V_GS = V_GD = 0; the
* gate-bulk voltage is the junction bias, with negligible effect), and only the junctions conduct. The junction size is the header's
* area/perimeter (AD/PD for di_bd, AS/PS for di_bs). AS is kept above 0 (1e-30) because the
* subcircuit recomputes the whole junction geometry from W and NF when as = 0, which would
* drop the header's drain area.
*
* The measured output "ib" of these files is the current at the junction-terminal SMU
* (header "ib I GROUND D SMU1" for di_bd, "ib I GROUND S SMU3" for di_bs), so the netlist
* reports the current into the swept junction terminal under that name.

*********
*Sources*
*********

.param VD={{ VD }}
.param VS={{ VS }}
.param VG={{ VG }}
.param VB={{ VB }}

Vd d 0 {VD}
Vs s 0 {VS}
Vg g 0 {VG}
Vb b 0 {VB}

*********
*Circuit*
*********

.param W={{ W }}
.param L={{ L }}
.param AD={{ AD }}
.param AS={{ AS if (AS|float) > 0 else "1e-30" }}
.param PD={{ PD }}
.param PS={{ PS }}
.param NF={{ NF }}
.param M={{ M }}

* D, G and S on the swept junction node ({{ sweep_node }}), bulk on its own source.
XU1 {{ sweep_node }} {{ sweep_node }} {{ sweep_node }} b {{ device_subckt }}
+ w={W} l={L} m={M} ng={NF} ad={AD} as={AS} pd={PD} ps={PS}

* ============================================================================================
* ----------------------------------------- ANALYSIS -----------------------------------------
* ============================================================================================

.temp {{ TEMP }}
* gmin far below the junction leakage: ngspice's default 1e-12 S per junction would add about
* 1e-11 A at 5 V, which is most of the measured reverse current of these structures.
.option gmin=1e-15

.control
  set filetype=ascii
  set wr_singlescale
  set wr_vecnames

  dc {{ sweep_var }} {{ sweep_start }} {{ sweep_stop }} {{ sweep_step }}

  * current into the junction terminal = what the junction SMU measured
  let ib = -i({{ sweep_var }})

  wrdata {{ out_path }} v({{ sweep_node }}) ib
  quit
.endc

* ============================================================================================
* ------------------------------------- CIR/MODELS-SETUP -------------------------------------
* ============================================================================================

.lib {{ model_corner_lib }} {{ corner }}

.end
